## Security Contract (non-negotiable)

{{ security_rules }}

**Additional frontend rules:**
- Never store auth tokens in localStorage — httpOnly cookies only (managed by backend)
- All user-generated content rendered as HTML must pass through `DOMPurify.sanitize()`
- No secrets, API keys, or internal URLs in frontend source code or build output
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix only for values safe to expose to the browser
- Route protection: all dashboard routes must check auth state and redirect to login if unauthenticated
- CSRF: rely on SameSite cookie configuration — do not add custom CSRF tokens unless security-model.md requires it

